---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { GOOGLE_RATING, pickVerifiedReviews } from '../data/reviews';

const aboutReviews = pickVerifiedReviews('about', 3);

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  "name": "About Dan Neale | Motion Story",
  "url": "https://motionstory.com.au/about/",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": ["h1", ".text-body"]
  },
  "mainEntity": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Dan Neale",
    "jobTitle": "Motion Designer & Creative Director",
    "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Motion Story" },
    "knowsAbout": [
      "Motion Design",
      "Creative Direction",
      "Storytelling",
      "Explainer Videos",
      "Product Videos",
      "Storyboarding",
      "SaaS Marketing",
      "Agency Creative Direction"
    ],
    "sameAs": [
      "https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielneale",
      "https://vimeo.com/wearemotionstory"
    ]
  }
};
---

<PageLayout
  title="About Dan Neale | Motion Story"
  description="Meet Dan Neale — the creative director and animator behind Motion Story. 1,000+ films since 2010, from the United Nations to TransferWise's first video. Byron Bay."
  activeNav="About"
  showCTA={false}
  floatSubject="About Motion Story"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://motionstory.com.au/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": "https://motionstory.com.au/about/" }
      ]
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="landing">
    <header class="landing-hero">
      <span class="landing-eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 class="landing-title">The person behind the films.</h1>
      <p class="landing-lede">I'm Dan Neale — creative director and animator. For sixteen years I've done one thing: taken ideas that are hard to explain and made films that make people understand and care.</p>
    </header>

    <p class="landing-clients">United Nations · TransferWise · Amex · Cartier · Atomic · Mosaic · RSPCA · Meltwater · Wipster</p>

    <!-- The story -->
    <section class="landing-section">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-16 items-start">
        <div>
          <div class="aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden mb-6">
            <img src="/daniel-neale.jpg" alt="Dan Neale, creative director of Motion Story" class="w-full h-full object-cover" loading="eager" />
          </div>
          <p class="text-metadata">Dan Neale</p>
          <p class="text-metadata opacity-40">Byron Bay, Australia</p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-8 max-w-2xl">
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            I trained as a graphic designer, and in 2010 I started animating — right as the explainer video became a thing. I've been making them since the category existed. Somewhere past the thousandth film, you stop counting and start noticing what actually makes people watch to the end: it's never the animation. It's the story underneath it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            That instinct has taken the work to some unusual places. The United Nations. TransferWise's first-ever video, working directly with their CEO. American Express, Cartier, state and federal government, and a long line of SaaS companies whose products were brilliant but invisible — software you can't point a camera at.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            I've run Motion Story the other way, too — with a scriptwriter, a producer, and a team of animators. It worked. But I watched what every layer between the client and the maker costs: the idea arrives diluted, the feedback arrives translated, and the budget goes to the layers instead of the film. So I stripped it back. Now the person you brief is the person who writes, storyboards, designs, and animates your film. No account managers, no juniors, no handoffs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            That means I take on a limited number of projects at a time, on purpose. It also means I'll challenge your brief before production starts — because clients don't hire me to execute silently, they hire me to find the story. The films get used to win investment, launch products, educate teams, and explain the things companies can't afford to have misunderstood.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            The rest of life is Byron Bay: I'm a father, a surfer, and a big-time animal lover. I put everything into the work — it's the only way I know how to do it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Career markers -->
    <section class="landing-section">
      <span class="landing-eyebrow landing-section-label">The short version</span>
      <div class="landing-cred">
        <div class="landing-cred-row">
          <h2 class="landing-cred-label">Since 2010</h2>
          <p class="landing-cred-body">1,000+ films. Making explainers since the category existed — trained as a graphic designer before that.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-cred-row">
          <h2 class="landing-cred-label">One maker</h2>
          <p class="landing-cred-body">I storyboard, design, illustrate, and animate — and I own the creative direction. Closer to a fractional creative partner than a vendor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-cred-row">
          <h2 class="landing-cred-label">Story first</h2>
          <p class="landing-cred-body">The script and structure get the same obsession as every frame. If the story is not strong, people do not watch to the end.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-cred-row">
          <h2 class="landing-cred-label">SaaS &amp; agencies</h2>
          <p class="landing-cred-body">Primary fit: software companies (including startups) and creative agencies that want senior motion and storytelling. White label or direct.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <span class="landing-eyebrow landing-section-label">What clients say</span>
      <p class="landing-clients" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        {GOOGLE_RATING.score} ★★★★★ on Google · {GOOGLE_RATING.count} reviews · <a href="/reviews/" style="border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;">All reviews</a>
      </p>
      <div class="landing-cred">
        {aboutReviews.map((review) => (
          <div class="landing-cred-row">
            <h3 class="landing-cred-label">{review.company}</h3>
            <p class="landing-cred-body">“{review.quote}” — {review.name}, {review.role}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <span class="landing-eyebrow landing-section-label">Questions</span>
      <div class="landing-faq">
        <div class="landing-faq-row">
          <h3 class="landing-faq-label">Cost</h3>
          <p class="text-body">From $5,000. I prefer projects around $10,000–$15,000. Fixed quote upfront.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-faq-row">
          <h3 class="landing-faq-label">Timeline</h3>
          <p class="text-body">Most projects take 3–6 weeks from kickoff to delivery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-faq-row">
          <h3 class="landing-faq-label">How I work</h3>
          <p class="text-body">Limited concurrent projects, on purpose. I challenge the brief before production. If you want silent execution with no questions, I am not the fit. If you want the story found and built properly, email me.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="landing-links" aria-label="Related pages">
      <a href="/work/" class="landing-link-card group">
        <span class="landing-eyebrow mb-4 block">Work</span>
        <p class="landing-link-label">See all work →</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/process/" class="landing-link-card group">
        <span class="landing-eyebrow mb-4 block">Process</span>
        <p class="landing-link-label">How I work →</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/explainer-videos/" class="landing-link-card group">
        <span class="landing-eyebrow mb-4 block">Explainers</span>
        <p class="landing-link-label">Explainer videos →</p>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
